	"department": "MUSIC",
	"description": [
		"In this course, students build an audition book of repertoire, surveying eras and genre-specific styles within the musical theater canon. Students develop an understanding of contemporary vocal styles unique to each repertoire category and practice techniques for both in-person and self-taped auditions according to industry standards. Coursework includes in-class and self-taped performances, goal-setting, and career preparation. Offered annually in Spring semester. Prerequisite: MUSPF 152 or MUSIC 148."
